question_stem:
A small ball is dropped from rest from height $h_1$ above the ground and falls vertically downwards. The ball collides with the ground and bounces back vertically upwards, reaching a maximum height $h_2$. Fig. 4.1 shows the ball just before and just after hitting the ground.

{{figure:figure_4_1}}

The ball has mass $0.25\text{ kg}$ and is in contact with the ground for a time of $0.18\text{ s}$. Just before the ball hits the ground, it has speed $5.2\text{ m s}^{-1}$. Just after it leaves the ground, it has speed $3.6\text{ m s}^{-1}$. Air resistance acting on the ball is negligible.
